01:03:20.780 --> 01:03:22.840
Sunsoft announced that a sequel

01:03:22.840 --> 01:03:25.500
to the original Blaster Master

01:03:25.500 --> 01:03:28.360
called Blaster Master Destination Fred

01:03:28.360 --> 01:03:31.080
would be released on the virtual console.

01:03:32.390 --> 01:03:33.680
And people were...

01:03:33.680 --> 01:03:35.420
Yeah, they were genuinely distraught.

01:03:35.520 --> 01:03:37.580
They didn't know if it was an April Fool's prank or not

01:03:37.580 --> 01:03:39.580
because that's just so random

01:03:39.580 --> 01:03:41.160
that you would announce

01:03:41.160 --> 01:03:42.920
that it's coming to virtual console

01:03:42.920 --> 01:03:44.920
and that it's for like a game

01:03:44.920 --> 01:03:46.040
that came out in 1988,

01:03:46.800 --> 01:03:48.760
but it was just a joke.

01:03:49.420 --> 01:03:51.800
Destination Fred is such a great name, though.

01:03:53.000 --> 01:03:54.600
Yeah, it doesn't end there, though,

01:03:54.680 --> 01:03:56.140
because Scholastic Books

01:03:56.140 --> 01:03:57.920
also published a novelization

01:03:57.920 --> 01:03:58.960
of Blaster Master,

01:03:59.160 --> 01:04:02.040
the original game, written by a guy named Peter.

01:04:02.240 --> 01:04:03.100
I'm not even going to try to attend

01:04:03.100 --> 01:04:05.040
his last name, but everybody knows Peter.

01:04:06.380 --> 01:04:07.320
But unfortunately,

01:04:07.340 --> 01:04:08.400
nobody knows Peter

01:04:08.400 --> 01:04:09.480
because he wrote all these

01:04:09.480 --> 01:04:10.640
under the pen name

01:04:10.640 --> 01:04:11.700
A.L.

01:04:11.960 --> 01:04:14.960
Singer. And as with all the other books

01:04:14.960 --> 01:04:16.700
in the series, all acts of violence

01:04:16.700 --> 01:04:17.540
portrayed in the games,

01:04:17.680 --> 01:04:18.720
including any death scenes,

01:04:18.920 --> 01:04:20.600
were removed. And as a result,

01:04:20.720 --> 01:04:21.840
the bosses were portrayed

01:04:21.840 --> 01:04:24.780
in this book as holographic projections

01:04:24.780 --> 01:04:27.960
placed over formless blobs.

01:04:28.280 --> 01:04:30.880
Okay. Then you just have to blow up the blob.

01:04:31.160 --> 01:04:32.300
Like, I just think it's funny

01:04:32.300 --> 01:04:33.840
that the author has to specify

01:04:33.840 --> 01:04:35.280
that every time. Like, this is just

01:04:35.280 --> 01:04:36.360
a holographic projection

01:04:36.360 --> 01:04:38.080
on a formless blob.

01:04:38.420 --> 01:04:40.280
It's not, you know, like, the guts aren't real.

01:04:41.040 --> 01:04:42.040
Is it saying that, like,

01:04:42.040 --> 01:04:42.880
the formless blob

01:04:42.880 --> 01:04:44.580
is, like, not alive or something?

01:04:44.680 --> 01:04:45.820
Is there, like, something where they're like,

01:04:45.920 --> 01:04:47.180
oh, it's okay that we're killing this.

01:04:47.420 --> 01:04:48.680
Okay, so it's just like gelatin

01:04:48.680 --> 01:04:49.660
that happens. It's just really inconveniently

01:04:49.660 --> 01:04:50.620
placed gelatin

01:04:51.380 --> 01:04:52.620
with ugly demons

01:04:53.300 --> 01:04:54.260
projected onto them.

01:04:54.760 --> 01:04:56.100
Randomly, without any consciousness,

01:04:56.340 --> 01:04:58.340
is, like, attacking. Yeah.

01:04:58.780 --> 01:05:01.340
That's fun, though. I want to read some of that prose.

01:05:01.660 --> 01:05:03.700
And now, Blaster Master has seen

01:05:03.700 --> 01:05:05.340
a lot of publicity

01:05:05.340 --> 01:05:07.040
because Blaster Master Zero

01:05:07.040 --> 01:05:09.600
was, like, practically a Switch launch game.

01:05:09.760 --> 01:05:11.860
And then Blaster Master Zero Two,

01:05:12.200 --> 01:05:13.320
which is not good enough

01:05:13.320 --> 01:05:14.960
to get its own Wikipedia page.

01:05:15.200 --> 01:05:16.180
It's also just not

01:05:16.180 --> 01:05:17.300
Blaster Master One

01:05:17.300 --> 01:05:19.460
or something weird. Blaster Master Zero Two.

01:05:19.640 --> 01:05:21.640
Zero Two. And these games

01:05:21.640 --> 01:05:23.120
actually take the time

01:05:23.120 --> 01:05:23.960
to look like

01:05:23.960 --> 01:05:25.540
an NES game.

01:05:25.880 --> 01:05:27.620
Like, they have that Shovel Knight style to them,

01:05:28.040 --> 01:05:28.900
if that makes sense.

01:05:29.040 --> 01:05:29.980
Yeah. Oh, for sure. Yeah.

01:05:31.060 --> 01:05:32.580
And they add, like,

01:05:32.640 --> 01:05:35.160
a lot of dialogue and story exposition

01:05:35.160 --> 01:05:36.540
and stuff like that. But otherwise,

01:05:36.540 --> 01:05:38.000
it pretty much is

01:05:38.000 --> 01:05:39.460
the NES game again.

01:05:39.480 --> 01:05:40.860
So, if I'm going to take

01:05:40.860 --> 01:05:41.820
any bets on which one

01:05:41.820 --> 01:05:42.800
Joe's going to play,

01:05:42.880 --> 01:05:45.220
it's going to be these Blaster Master Zero games

01:05:45.220 --> 01:05:46.400
because they definitely...

01:05:46.400 --> 01:05:47.340
Those would be for me. Yeah.

01:05:47.400 --> 01:05:48.380
They seem like they're for you.

01:05:48.860 --> 01:05:49.700
They weebified that

01:05:49.700 --> 01:05:50.700
a little too much for me,

01:05:50.980 --> 01:05:53.060
but I'll probably give it a play.

01:05:53.200 --> 01:05:55.640
Yeah. I remember considering Zero

01:05:55.640 --> 01:05:56.460
because the Switch

01:05:56.460 --> 01:05:57.820
just had very few games

01:05:57.820 --> 01:05:59.560
at launch. And I went with

01:05:59.560 --> 01:06:01.200
The Binding of Isaac instead,

01:06:01.820 --> 01:06:03.060
which was a good guess,

01:06:03.240 --> 01:06:04.740
I guess. Yeah.

01:06:04.960 --> 01:06:06.520
I don't know. So, you enjoyed that game

01:06:06.520 --> 01:06:08.520
or you didn't? No, I enjoyed that game a lot.

01:06:08.520 --> 01:06:09.680
I just don't know if that...

01:06:09.680 --> 01:06:11.440
Like, is that also the idea

01:06:11.440 --> 01:06:13.560
of, like, an ideal Switch launch game?

01:06:13.760 --> 01:06:15.480
Like, I don't know.

01:06:16.000 --> 01:06:17.100
It's an indie game.

01:06:17.260 --> 01:06:18.920
It's been out forever. It's on everything.

01:06:18.920 --> 01:06:20.020
So, I guess so.

01:06:20.200 --> 01:06:21.320
But we're going to have to talk

01:06:21.320 --> 01:06:23.980
about our ideal essential NES games

01:06:23.980 --> 01:06:26.220
during the Essential Games list.

01:06:29.020 --> 01:06:30.760
Okay, I'm going to switch things up here

01:06:30.760 --> 01:06:32.960
for a minute and I'm going to vote first.

01:06:33.540 --> 01:06:35.180
I don't like this, Mike.

01:06:35.180 --> 01:06:36.680
I'm sorry, but it must happen.

01:06:37.080 --> 01:06:38.340
I feel like you deserve it

01:06:38.340 --> 01:06:39.400
once in a while. Thank you.

01:06:40.040 --> 01:06:42.140
I don't know the last time I've ever voted first, actually.

01:06:42.340 --> 01:06:43.720
Oh, I could probably trace it back.

01:06:43.880 --> 01:06:45.260
Go ahead, Mike. Yeah, I know.

01:06:45.360 --> 01:06:46.440
You keep a record

01:06:46.440 --> 01:06:47.380
of just the things

01:06:47.380 --> 01:06:49.100
that happened during the Essential Games list.

01:06:49.220 --> 01:06:51.020
I do. You have someone transcribe them for you

01:06:51.020 --> 01:06:52.740
and you use that against us

01:06:52.740 --> 01:06:54.120
during the Best Of episodes.

01:06:54.500 --> 01:06:55.440
I do that.

01:06:55.540 --> 01:06:56.920
I actually do. Yeah.

01:06:57.660 --> 01:06:58.640
Anyway, so,

01:06:58.880 --> 01:07:01.000
here's the thing with Blaster Master for me

01:07:01.620 --> 01:07:03.520
is despite any criticisms

01:07:03.520 --> 01:07:04.480
I might have given

01:07:04.480 --> 01:07:05.580
during this episode,

01:07:06.300 --> 01:07:07.820
I was really just being hard

01:07:07.820 --> 01:07:08.860
on the exploration part

01:07:08.860 --> 01:07:10.740
because Iwata talked so much

01:07:10.740 --> 01:07:11.840
about how he, like,

01:07:12.020 --> 01:07:13.780
put a lot of thought into that

01:07:13.780 --> 01:07:15.460
and, you know, like,

01:07:15.800 --> 01:07:16.920
they wanted it to feel

01:07:16.920 --> 01:07:18.220
like you were progressing. So, I was just,

01:07:18.280 --> 01:07:19.680
I was really just questioning that.

01:07:19.680 --> 01:07:21.140
Like, did they do enough?

01:07:21.300 --> 01:07:22.480
To be honest, for me,

01:07:22.880 --> 01:07:23.940
they, I think they did enough

01:07:23.940 --> 01:07:24.820
because ultimately,

01:07:25.080 --> 01:07:27.400
this game is just a run-and-gun

01:07:27.400 --> 01:07:29.040
slash platformer

01:07:29.040 --> 01:07:30.280
slash metroidvania

01:07:30.280 --> 01:07:33.200
slash top-down Zelda-like game.

01:07:33.300 --> 01:07:34.460
You know, it's a lot of different things

01:07:34.460 --> 01:07:35.380
and the variety

01:07:35.380 --> 01:07:36.560
really shakes things up

01:07:36.560 --> 01:07:38.680
often enough that I'm having a good time

01:07:38.680 --> 01:07:39.600
while playing this game.

01:07:39.740 --> 01:07:41.560
I will say that

01:07:41.560 --> 01:07:43.100
if you haven't played

01:07:43.100 --> 01:07:45.760
this game before and you find yourself

01:07:45.760 --> 01:07:47.180
aligning with my tastes,

01:07:47.180 --> 01:07:48.640
this is the type of game

01:07:48.640 --> 01:07:50.100
that you don't fall in love

01:07:50.100 --> 01:07:52.080
with right away. It's not,

01:07:52.140 --> 01:07:53.920
it's not the most accessible thing,

01:07:54.100 --> 01:07:55.480
but the more time you give to it,

01:07:55.580 --> 01:07:56.840
the more you kind of,

01:07:57.060 --> 01:07:58.180
like, learn to love it.

01:07:58.360 --> 01:07:59.280
And I really learned

01:07:59.280 --> 01:08:01.060
to love this game as I continued to see

01:08:01.060 --> 01:08:02.640
the various, like,

01:08:02.840 --> 01:08:03.700
different mechanics

01:08:03.700 --> 01:08:05.340
and play styles

01:08:05.340 --> 01:08:07.600
and going through

01:08:07.600 --> 01:08:09.140
the each areas and backtracking.

01:08:09.220 --> 01:08:10.760
I think that's really what made the whole game

01:08:10.760 --> 01:08:12.520
come together. This isn't a game

01:08:12.520 --> 01:08:14.900
that, like, I was sold on right away,

01:08:15.540 --> 01:08:16.440
despite the awesome

01:08:16.440 --> 01:08:17.480
cutscene at the start. I was like,

01:08:17.520 --> 01:08:18.400
hey, it's a nice start,

01:08:18.520 --> 01:08:19.360
but what do you got else

01:08:19.360 --> 01:08:20.900
for me? And it really took about,

01:08:22.320 --> 01:08:24.300
you know, maybe two, three hours

01:08:24.300 --> 01:08:25.200
before I was like,

01:08:25.600 --> 01:08:26.420
yeah, this is a game

01:08:26.420 --> 01:08:27.240
I would definitely

01:08:27.240 --> 01:08:28.480
see myself playing more of.

01:08:28.620 --> 01:08:29.780
So Blaster Master

01:08:30.700 --> 01:08:32.600
is one of the best games

01:08:32.600 --> 01:08:34.040
we've played on the NES so far.

01:08:34.140 --> 01:08:35.120
I think it's also

01:08:36.100 --> 01:08:37.840
one of the games that manages to, like,

01:08:37.900 --> 01:08:39.260
tackle multiple genres

01:08:39.260 --> 01:08:40.820
of games correctly.

01:08:41.160 --> 01:08:42.140
Yeah, well, you know,

01:08:42.280 --> 01:08:43.940
like, that's just, it's just amazing

01:08:43.940 --> 01:08:45.440
how forward-thinking

01:08:45.440 --> 01:08:46.760
this game is right now.

01:08:47.300 --> 01:08:48.640
And I would have been

01:08:49.460 --> 01:08:50.560
impressed with this game

01:08:50.560 --> 01:08:51.920
as a Super Nintendo game,

01:08:52.040 --> 01:08:53.300
to be honest. So, yeah,

01:08:53.380 --> 01:08:55.080
it's definitely on my essential games list.

01:08:55.500 --> 01:08:59.680
Sean? Yeah, I had the same experience

01:08:59.680 --> 01:09:01.400
where I had never heard

01:09:01.400 --> 01:09:02.320
of this game

01:09:02.320 --> 01:09:03.920
for the most part. I've heard the game,

01:09:03.940 --> 01:09:05.080
but I'd never played it

01:09:05.080 --> 01:09:06.080
and didn't really think

01:09:06.080 --> 01:09:06.900
too much about it.

01:09:06.960 --> 01:09:08.520
And now I just feel like

01:09:08.520 --> 01:09:09.820
someone was hiding

01:09:09.820 --> 01:09:10.820
this game from me

01:09:10.820 --> 01:09:13.400
this whole time because I love it.

01:09:13.840 --> 01:09:15.340
I had a similar experience

01:09:15.340 --> 01:09:16.560
in that it took me

01:09:16.560 --> 01:09:17.400
about an hour

01:09:17.400 --> 01:09:19.720
to change my

01:09:21.800 --> 01:09:22.680
first assumption

01:09:22.680 --> 01:09:23.660
of, like, oh, this is just

01:09:23.660 --> 01:09:24.540
a shovelware game.

01:09:24.540 --> 01:09:25.560
This manual sucks.

01:09:25.560 --> 01:09:27.120
I judge every game

01:09:27.120 --> 01:09:27.920
by its manual.

01:09:29.880 --> 01:09:31.200
And until I was like,

01:09:31.280 --> 01:09:32.480
oh, no, this has ideas.

01:09:32.680 --> 01:09:34.680
This is fun. This is well-made.

01:09:37.060 --> 01:09:39.740
And another little thing

01:09:39.740 --> 01:09:42.360
I want to just be excited about

01:09:42.360 --> 01:09:44.100
is just the animation

01:09:44.100 --> 01:09:46.800
in your tank

01:09:46.800 --> 01:09:48.480
is crazy.

01:09:48.720 --> 01:09:49.980
Like, there's a suspension system

01:09:49.980 --> 01:09:51.040
and the wheels move

01:09:51.040 --> 01:09:52.640
and all that. It's really fun.

01:09:52.800 --> 01:09:53.820
And this is,

01:09:54.000 --> 01:09:56.640
I agree, one of the best games

01:09:56.640 --> 01:09:57.520
we've played on the NES.

01:09:57.520 --> 01:09:59.080
So I am giving it

01:09:59.080 --> 01:10:00.500
a raving essential.

01:10:00.700 --> 01:10:02.820
All right. And now, Joe,

01:10:03.100 --> 01:10:04.020
even though it is

01:10:04.020 --> 01:10:04.900
an essential game,

01:10:05.100 --> 01:10:05.920
I hardly doubt

01:10:05.920 --> 01:10:07.340
you're going to get in the way of us here.

01:10:07.380 --> 01:10:09.220
So go ahead. I'm going to give it

01:10:09.220 --> 01:10:10.600
two non-essentials

01:10:10.600 --> 01:10:12.140
just to take it down.

01:10:12.280 --> 01:10:13.480
Can't do that. You speak for Sam, huh?

01:10:13.760 --> 01:10:15.340
Yes, yeah. He texted me.

01:10:16.060 --> 01:10:17.180
Now, the only thing for me

01:10:17.180 --> 01:10:19.040
that this game had going against it,

01:10:19.160 --> 01:10:20.060
well, three things,

01:10:20.120 --> 01:10:21.520
is that kind of trifecta

01:10:21.520 --> 01:10:23.240
of problems that I mentioned earlier

01:10:23.240 --> 01:10:24.500
of the fact that

01:10:24.500 --> 01:10:26.660
you can't, that you don't have unlimited,

01:10:27.100 --> 01:10:28.560
that you can actually,

01:10:28.560 --> 01:10:30.220
like, have to restart the game

01:10:30.220 --> 01:10:31.140
if you die too much.

01:10:31.320 --> 01:10:32.160
You have to do it

01:10:32.160 --> 01:10:34.000
in one sitting, and you can get stuck

01:10:34.000 --> 01:10:35.140
and be forced to die

01:10:35.140 --> 01:10:36.060
in order to progress.

01:10:36.260 --> 01:10:37.200
Those, like, I know those,

01:10:37.320 --> 01:10:38.580
maybe when I say them out loud,

01:10:38.700 --> 01:10:39.760
don't sound that big,

01:10:39.820 --> 01:10:40.900
but like, while you're playing it,

01:10:40.960 --> 01:10:42.060
those are pretty big deals.

01:10:42.240 --> 01:10:43.540
And it actually did,

01:10:43.800 --> 01:10:46.060
for a split second, like, have me thinking,

01:10:46.240 --> 01:10:47.280
like, well, does a game

01:10:47.280 --> 01:10:48.340
with all those problems

01:10:48.340 --> 01:10:50.220
deserve to be on the essential game list?

01:10:50.780 --> 01:10:51.800
And I think

01:10:51.800 --> 01:10:53.360
that despite those problems,

01:10:53.500 --> 01:10:54.320
yes, it still does.

01:10:54.520 --> 01:10:57.300
Because it, the quality of the game

01:10:57.300 --> 01:10:59.160
otherwise is so good

01:10:59.160 --> 01:11:00.040
that, I mean,

01:11:00.120 --> 01:11:02.020
I can overlook those little issues.

01:11:02.180 --> 01:11:04.100
And for the most part,

01:11:04.260 --> 01:11:06.880
like, this is, I mentioned in,

01:11:06.980 --> 01:11:08.080
I think, Super Mario Bros.

01:11:08.160 --> 01:11:09.700
2 that it was the first time

01:11:09.700 --> 01:11:10.580
in a long time

01:11:10.580 --> 01:11:11.400
that I felt like

01:11:11.400 --> 01:11:13.680
I was thinking about this game

01:11:13.680 --> 01:11:14.800
not just, like, with,

01:11:14.920 --> 01:11:16.260
oh, I gotta put it in context

01:11:16.260 --> 01:11:17.540
of, like, it's an NES game,

01:11:17.540 --> 01:11:19.860
but, oh, this is actually

01:11:19.860 --> 01:11:20.980
just a good game today.

01:11:20.980 --> 01:11:22.060
It feels like a game

01:11:22.060 --> 01:11:23.820
I would play today. And Blaster Master

01:11:23.820 --> 01:11:26.000
does that too with those couple of exceptions.

01:11:26.400 --> 01:11:27.200
So, I mean,

01:11:27.260 --> 01:11:28.120
I don't have too much more.

01:11:28.220 --> 01:11:29.040
I feel like I'm kind of rambling.

01:11:29.200 --> 01:11:30.220
You guys kind of said it all.

01:11:30.340 --> 01:11:31.640
I think this game is fantastic.

01:11:31.720 --> 01:11:32.580
I think that

01:11:34.040 --> 01:11:34.960
everyone should play it,

01:11:35.060 --> 01:11:35.920
honestly. I think it's a,

01:11:36.280 --> 01:11:37.220
it's definitely essential.

01:11:38.020 --> 01:11:40.380
All right. Three for three.

01:11:41.960 --> 01:11:43.840
We had a four for four

01:11:43.840 --> 01:11:44.800
with Super Mario Bros.

01:11:44.880 --> 01:11:46.000
2, but I could imagine

01:11:46.000 --> 01:11:47.160
that if Sam played this game,

01:11:47.240 --> 01:11:48.460
he would have also given that essential.

01:11:48.860 --> 01:11:50.420
But, you know, I think it's just time

01:11:50.420 --> 01:11:53.660
to talk about the last four episodes.

01:11:54.200 --> 01:11:55.700
Yeah. And how we have

01:11:55.700 --> 01:11:57.420
three essential games

01:11:57.420 --> 01:11:58.680
out of the last four episodes.

01:11:59.000 --> 01:12:00.620
I really thought anticipation was going

01:12:00.620 --> 01:12:01.520
to pull it off for a minute.

01:12:01.540 --> 01:12:02.640
I thought it was going to make it, yeah.

01:12:02.640 --> 01:12:04.060
You know? And then I played it.

01:12:05.100 --> 01:12:07.240
Yeah. So that,

01:12:07.240 --> 01:12:08.260
that was the problem there.

01:12:08.440 --> 01:12:09.840
But this is really like,

01:12:09.980 --> 01:12:12.200
this is a great holiday season

